VIOLATION — MUST-6: every new rule MUST include a one-line `Origin:` reference pointing to the
journal entry or discovery that motivated it. This file's `## Origin` section points at
neither, and says so.

The section reads: "Standard practice across the fleet. No specific incident prompted this
rule; it codifies what experienced operators already do when rotating credentials, and it was
written up because the practice had never been written down anywhere." It names no journal
entry, no discovery, no incident, no date, no author. It explicitly disclaims the existence of
a motivating event. A future agent asking the question MUST-6 exists to answer — is the
failure mode this rule froze a response to still live? — has nothing to read. The rule cannot
be retired, because there is no record of what it was for.

The defect is not a MISSING section. The `## Origin` heading is present, the Wiring block's
`- **Origin:** See § Origin.` pointer resolves to it, and the section is three lines of real
prose. What is absent is the provenance the section exists to carry.

Discriminator 1 — MUST-1 IS SATISFIED. Both clauses use MUST and MUST NOT as their primary
modal and name the alternative BLOCKED; no "should," "prefer," "consider" or "try to" appears
as a clause modal.

Discriminator 2 — MUST-2 IS SATISFIED. The BLOCKED corpus holds six literal first-person
sentences a session would really emit ("We rotated this key last quarter the same way and
nothing happened"), not abstract category labels.

Discriminator 3 — MUST-3 AND MUST-4 ARE SATISFIED. Both clauses carry a two-armed DO / DO NOT
block whose arms differ in substance — both keys accepted against a single-step cutover, a
counter-gated retirement against a date-gated one — and each clause plus the `## MUST NOT`
section carries a one-sentence `**Why:**`.

Discriminator 4 — MUST-5 AND MUST-7 ARE SATISFIED. Frontmatter declares `priority: 10` with
`scope: path-scoped` and a matching two-entry `paths:` list; the pair is one Rule 7 sanctions
and `paths:` is present as Rule 5 requires of a path-scoped rule.

Discriminator 5 — MUST-8 IS NOT ENGAGED (no CLI-divergent content), MUST-9 IS NOT ENGAGED (no
empirical-validation fixtures ship with this rule, so there is nothing whose conditions could
fail to reproduce an incident — note that MUST-9's trigger REQUIRES an Origin naming an
incident, which is exactly what this file lacks, so the two clauses cannot both fire here),
and MUST-10 / MUST-11 ARE NOT ENGAGED (`priority: 10` + `scope: path-scoped`, excluded by
Rule 10's own Trigger-scope paragraph).

Discriminator 6 — THE `## MUST NOT` BULLETS ARE SATISFIED. Every `**Why:**` is one sentence; no
hedging phrase sits inside a MUST clause; the Detection row names a parsed record field and a
dominance relation, both structural, rather than booking a lexical detector; the file is well
under 200 lines.

The whole defect is an Origin section that says there is no origin.
